  "notes": "{掻|か}く means to scratch or scrape a surface, typically with fingernails. It is a godan verb with the pattern Xを{掻|か}く.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xを{掻|か}く\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{掻|か}いている describes the ongoing action of scratching.\n\nIDIOMS AND SET PHRASES:\n- {頭|あたま}を{掻|か}く: to scratch one's head (showing embarrassment or confusion)\n- {汗|あせ}を{掻|か}く: to sweat (note: different kanji/meaning)\n- {恥|はじ}を{掻|か}く: to be embarrassed, to lose face\n\nWATCH OUT:\nNot to be confused with other verbs read かく:\n- {書|か}く: to write\n- {描|か}く: to draw\n- {欠|か}く: to lack",
